{"id": "unknown-2026-11-03-009", "date": "2026-11-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Waaree doubles Texas solar module manufacturing capacity to 3.2 GW", "content": "<p>Waaree Solar Americas has started commercial production on two new 800 MW solar module manufacturing lines at its Brookshire facility in Texas, doubling the plant's annual production capacity.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/waaree-solar-americas-begins-commercial-production-on-1-6-gw-of-new-module-lines-doubling-texas-capacity-to-3-2-gw/\">Waaree doubles Texas solar module manufacturing capacity to 3.2 GW</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.c", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/waaree-solar-americas-begins-commercial-production-on-1-6-gw-of-new-module-lines-doubling-texas-capacity-to-3-2-gw/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-03-010", "date": "2026-11-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Germany awards 288 MW of solar in rooftop tender at average price of €0.0967/kWh", "content": "<p>Germany’s latest rooftop solar tender received 177 bids totaling 347 MW, with 108 bids representing 208 MW ultimately awarded contracts. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/germany-awards-288-mw-of-solar-in-rooftop-tender-at-average-price-of-e0-0967-kwh/\">Germany awards 288 MW of solar in rooftop tender at average price of €0.0967/kWh</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/germany-awards-288-mw-of-solar-in-rooftop-tender-at-average-price-of-e0-0967-kwh/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-03-011", "date": "2026-11-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Key takeaways from All Energy Australia 2026", "content": "<p>The outlook for Australia’s renewable energy transition appears positive with supportive government policies and renewable energy targets, a surge in battery installations, and a strong pipeline of grid-scale solar and storage projects helping to fuel confidence.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/batteries-are-big-at-all-energy-australia-2026/\">Key takeaways from All Energy Australia 2026</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Glo", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/batteries-are-big-at-all-energy-australia-2026/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-03-012", "date": "2026-11-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["grid_parity", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solar PV cuts Spain’s electricity costs by €17.02 billion over 18 months", "content": "<p>A study by Spanish solar association UNEF estimates that solar PV generation reduced Spain’s wholesale electricity costs by €17.02 billion ($19.03 billion) between January 2025 and June 2026. Without solar generation, average daily market prices would have been 86% higher, according to the analysis.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/solar-pv-cuts-spains-electricity-costs-by-e17-02-billion-over-18-months/\">Solar PV cuts Spain’s electricity costs by €17.02 billion ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/solar-pv-cuts-spains-electricity-costs-by-e17-02-billion-over-18-months/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-03-013", "date": "2026-11-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Slovenia tenders solar-plus-storage project", "content": "<p>A tender is open in Slovenia for the development of a solar-plus-storage project at a former waste landfill site. The deadline for applications is November 19.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/slovenia-tenders-solar-plus-storage-project/\">Slovenia tenders solar-plus-storage project</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/slovenia-tenders-solar-plus-storage-project/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "trina-2026-11-03-014", "date": "2026-11-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": ["trina"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Shenzhen Nanshan Power seeks majority stake in Trina Solar’s tracker business", "content": "<p>Shenzhen Nanshan Power plans to acquire a 51% to 70% stake in Trina Solar’s tracker business through a cash transaction. The proposed deal could provide Trina Solar with additional capital as it navigates financial pressure and intensifying competition in China’s solar sector.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/shenzhen-nanshan-power-seeks-majority-stake-in-trina-solars-tracker-business/\">Shenzhen Nanshan Power seeks majority stake in Trina Solar’s tracker busines", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/shenzhen-nanshan-power-seeks-majority-stake-in-trina-solars-tracker-business/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-03-015", "date": "2026-11-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Yingfa Ruineng establishes 7.5 GW PV manufacturing plant in Indonesia", "content": "<p>The facility is the Chinese manufacturer's first overseas base. It will produce n-type TOPCon solar cells for Indonesia’s domestic market while also acting as a regional supply hub for Southeast Asia and the Middle East.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/yingfa-ruineng-establishes-7-5-gw-pv-manufacturing-plant-in-indonesia/\">Yingfa Ruineng establishes 7.5 GW PV manufacturing plant in Indonesia</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazin", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/yingfa-ruineng-establishes-7-5-gw-pv-manufacturing-plant-in-indonesia/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-03-016", "date": "2026-11-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Behind-the-meter generation could deliver five times more grid relief than data center load shifting", "content": "<p>An Ember analysis finds that data center load shifting could reduce peak electricity demand by up to 1.5% in Ireland by 2030, offering limited grid flexibility. Behind-the-meter generation and storage could provide nearly five times more relief, with potential reductions of up to 2.7 GW in Texas.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/behind-the-meter-generation-could-deliver-five-times-more-grid-relief-than-data-center-load-shifting/\">Behind-the-meter generation coul", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/behind-the-meter-generation-could-deliver-five-times-more-grid-relief-than-data-center-load-shifting/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-03-017", "date": "2026-11-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Hybrid wind-solar-battery plants can power Kazakhstan’s demand growth", "content": "<p>Ember analysis finds that hybrid wind, solar and battery plants could supply electricity at an average cost of $56/MWh in Kazakhstan, compared with $70–170/MWh for new coal, while meeting up to 90% of typical demand.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/hybrid-wind-solar-battery-plants-can-power-kazakhstans-demand-growth/\">Hybrid wind-solar-battery plants can power Kazakhstan’s demand growth</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Glo", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/hybrid-wind-solar-battery-plants-can-power-kazakhstans-demand-growth/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-03-018", "date": "2026-11-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Planar heat pipes reduce peak temperatures by up to 32 C in PV cooling tests", "content": "<p>An international research team has tested five planar heat pipe designs for PV module cooling, achieving peak surface temperature reductions of 8 C to 32 C. The researchers estimated that active water cooling could increase annual electricity generation by 2.2% to 3.6% under conditions in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/planar-heat-pipes-reduce-peak-temperatures-by-up-to-32-c-in-pv-cooling-tests/\">Planar heat pipes reduce peak temperatures", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/03/planar-heat-pipes-reduce-peak-temperatures-by-up-to-32-c-in-pv-cooling-tests/", "type": "rss"}]}
